## Features

- **Authentication:** register and login with JWT (access and refresh tokens), automatic token refresh, protected routes.
- **Kanban board:** Applied, Interview, Offer and Rejected columns. Drag a card to change its status (saved instantly with optimistic UI updates).
- **Application CRUD:** add and delete applications with company, role and notes.
- **Search and filters:** search across company, role and notes; filter by status; order and paginate results.
- **Dashboard:** totals, interviews, offers, success rate and a bar chart of applications per status.
- **AI match:** paste a job description and either paste your resume text or upload a PDF. Gemini returns a match score, matched skills, missing skills and suggestions.
- **Per-user data isolation:** every user only ever sees their own applications.

---

## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, TanStack React Query, Axios, @hello-pangea/dnd, Recharts |
| Backend | Python, Django 5, Django REST Framework, SimpleJWT, django-cors-headers |
| Database | MySQL (PyMySQL driver) |
| AI | Google Gemini API, pypdf for PDF text extraction |
| Deployment | Vercel (frontend), Render (Django with Gunicorn and WhiteNoise), Aiven (managed MySQL) |

---

## Architecture

```
Browser (Next.js on Vercel)
   |  HTTPS + JSON, Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
   v
Django REST API (Render)
   |-- CORS middleware        -> allows only the frontend origin
   |-- JWT authentication     -> sets request.user
   |-- ViewSets + serializers -> validation and JSON conversion
   |-- Django ORM             -> SQL queries
   v
MySQL (Aiven)                  Gemini API (AI match endpoint)
```

---

## API endpoints

Base URL: `/api`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/auth/register/` | No | Create an account |
| POST | `/auth/login/` | No | Get `access` and `refresh` tokens |
| POST | `/auth/refresh/` | No | Get a new access token |
| GET | `/applications/` | Yes | List your applications. Supports `?search=`, `?status=`, `?ordering=`, `?page=` |
| POST | `/applications/` | Yes | Create an application |
| GET, PUT, PATCH, DELETE | `/applications/<id>/` | Yes | Read, replace, update or delete one application |
| GET | `/applications/stats/` | Yes | Totals and counts per status |
| POST | `/ai/match/` | Yes | Resume vs job description analysis (text or PDF) |

